('NZ:early-childhood-teacher','2026-08-11',null,39.66,82500,15,0,0,0,10,8,0,8,1,42,'career-opportunity-nz-v1','provisional',jsonb_build_object('classification_scope','ANZSCO 241111 Early Childhood (Pre-primary School) Teacher — registered.','shortage_note','Current Green List Tier 2 status is used as direct policy-demand evidence; 15/20.','visa_basis','Green List Tier 2 Work to Residence when Teaching Council registration/certification and current requirements are met; 8/10.','salary_method','Midpoint of Tahatū current most-common Early Childhood Teacher annual pay range NZD 72,000-93,000; 8/10.','entry_basis','Recognised early-childhood teaching degree or graduate diploma, typically 3-4 years for direct undergraduate entry; 10/15.','entry_burden_basis','Teaching Council registration plus a current practising certificate are required to officially teach; 1/5.'),'2026-08-11'),
('NZ:primary-school-teacher','2026-08-11',null,39.66,82500,20,0,0,0,10,8,0,10,1,49,'career-opportunity-nz-v1','provisional',jsonb_build_object('classification_scope','ANZSCO 241213 Primary School Teacher. Māori-medium and intermediate teacher codes are not rolled into the canonical primary profile.','shortage_note','Current Green List Tier 1 status is used as the strongest direct policy-demand signal; 20/20.','visa_basis','Green List Tier 1 Straight to Residence when Teaching Council registration/certification and current requirements are met; 10/10.','salary_method','Midpoint of Tahatū current most-common Primary School Teacher annual pay range NZD 72,000-93,000; 8/10.','entry_basis','Bachelor of primary teaching or graduate/postgraduate initial-teacher-education route; 10/15.','entry_burden_basis','Teaching Council registration and a current practising certificate are required; 1/5.'),'2026-08-11'),
('NZ:secondary-school-teacher','2026-08-11',null,39.66,82500,20,0,0,0,10,8,0,10,1,49,'career-opportunity-nz-v1','provisional',jsonb_build_object('classification_scope','ANZSCO 241411 Secondary School Teacher.','shortage_note','Current Green List Tier 1 status is used as the strongest direct policy-demand signal; 20/20.','visa_basis','Green List Tier 1 Straight to Residence when Teaching Council registration/certification and current requirements are met; 10/10.','salary_method','Midpoint of Tahatū current most-common Secondary School Teacher annual pay range NZD 72,000-93,000; 8/10.','entry_basis','Recognised secondary teaching qualification plus one or more specialist subjects, typically 3-4 years of combined subject/teacher preparation; 10/15.','entry_burden_basis','Teaching Council registration and a current practising certificate are required; 1/5.'),'2026-08-11'),
('NZ:special-education-teacher','2026-08-11',null,39.66,82500,15,0,0,0,8,8,0,8,1,40,'career-opportunity-nz-v1','provisional',jsonb_build_object('classification_scope','ANZSCO 2415 roll-up: 241511 Special Needs Teacher, 241512 Teacher of the Hearing Impaired, 241513 Teacher of the Sight Impaired and 241599 Special Education Teachers nec.','shortage_note','These special-education teacher occupations are current Green List Tier 2; 15/20.','visa_basis','Green List Tier 2 Work to Residence when Teaching Council registration/certification and occupation requirements are met; 8/10.','salary_method','Tahatū does not publish a distinct special-education-teacher salary page in the reviewed layer, so the midpoint of its current registered school-teacher most-common range NZD 72,000-93,000 is used as a transparent teacher proxy; 8/10.','entry_basis','Initial teacher education plus learning-support/special-education expertise creates a more specialised route than general classroom teaching; 8/15.','entry_burden_basis','Teaching Council registration and a current practising certificate are required for the teacher scope; 1/5.'),'2026-08-11'),
('NZ:social-worker','2026-08-11',null,46.63,97000,20,0,0,0,8,8,0,10,1,47,'career-opportunity-nz-v1','provisional',jsonb_build_object('classification_scope','ANZSCO 272511 Social Worker.','shortage_note','Social Worker 272511 is on the current Green List Tier 1; 20/20.','visa_basis','Green List Tier 1 Straight to Residence when SWRB registration and qualification requirements are met; 10/10.','salary_method','Midpoint of Tahatū current most-common Social Worker annual pay range NZD 87,000-107,000; 8/10.','entry_basis','A recognised professional social-work qualification is required; Tahatū/SWRB pathways are degree-based and include supervised field education; 8/15.','entry_burden_basis','The title social worker is protected; SWRB registration and a current annual practising certificate are required to practise as a social worker; 1/5.','current_registration_note','The former section 13 experience-only registration pathway closed to new applications from 28 February 2026.'),'2026-08-11'),
('NZ:youth-worker','2026-08-11',null,32.69,68000,0,0,0,0,15,4,0,5,5,29,'career-opportunity-nz-v1','provisional',jsonb_build_object('classification_scope','ANZSCO 411716 Youth Worker.','shortage_note','No current Green List or recurring occupation-specific shortage credit is assigned.','visa_basis','Standard skilled-work treatment where the role and applicant meet current requirements; no dedicated Green List residence shortcut; 5/10.','salary_method','Midpoint of Tahatū current most-common Youth Worker annual pay range NZD 63,000-73,000; 4/10.','entry_basis','Certificate, diploma and degree routes exist and Tahatū describes 0-3 years of training with experience useful; 15/15.','entry_burden_basis','No statutory occupational registration is required; professional-organisation membership may be useful; 5/5.'),'2026-08-11'),
('NZ:community-worker','2026-08-11',null,26.50,55120,0,0,0,0,15,2,0,5,5,27,'career-opportunity-nz-v1','provisional',jsonb_build_object('classification_scope','ANZSCO 411711 Community Worker. Tahatū Support Worker is used only as the closest transparent pay/entry proxy because its current career page explicitly includes Community Worker as an alternative title.','shortage_note','No current Green List or recurring occupation-specific shortage credit is assigned.','visa_basis','Standard skilled-work treatment where a specific role satisfies current occupation and visa requirements; 5/10.','salary_method','Midpoint of Tahatū current most-common Support Worker hourly pay range NZD 25-28, annualised at 2,080 hours; 2/10.','entry_basis','On-the-job entry plus Level 2-4 Health and Wellbeing qualifications provide an accessible pathway for the reviewed support/community scope; 15/15.','entry_burden_basis','No statutory occupational registration is required; 5/5.'),'2026-08-11'),
('NZ:counsellor','2026-08-11',null,46.63,97000,20,0,0,0,10,8,0,10,4,52,'career-opportunity-nz-v1','provisional',jsonb_build_object('classification_scope','ANZSCO 2721 non-addiction counsellor roll-up: 272111 Careers Counsellor, 272113 Family and Marriage Counsellor, 272114 Rehabilitation Counsellor, 272115 Student Counsellor and 272199 Counsellors nec. Drug and Alcohol Counsellor 272112 is excluded because its Green List credential pathway is Dapaanz-specific.','shortage_note','The reviewed non-addiction counsellor codes are current Green List Tier 1 occupations; 20/20.','visa_basis','Green List Tier 1 Straight to Residence requires New Zealand Association of Counsellors membership and the listed qualification pathway for these counsellor occupations; 10/10.','salary_method','Midpoint of Tahatū current most-common Counsellor annual pay range NZD 87,000-107,000; 8/10.','entry_basis','Bachelor-level counselling study is the normal direct route, with postgraduate study common in some specialties; 10/15.','entry_burden_basis','Counselling is not treated as a universally statutorily registered profession in the profile, but NZAC membership is a specific Green List requirement and materially constrains the residence pathway; 4/5.'),'2026-08-11')
